// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Plant_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P810284717" "These horrid perversions of normal flora have become one of the most identifiable monsters in the Devouring Earth's maniacal menagerie. In addition to their astonishing mobility, they can fire swarms of thorns at their enemies, tearing flesh to shreds in an instant."
// DisplayNames :
"P2520576911" "Bladegrass"
// DisplayNames :
"P1538293807" "Razorvine"
// DisplayNames :
"P1729998282" "Blackrose"
// DisplayNames :
"P2138175364" "Deathblossom"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Plant_Beast_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1009925835" "The older, more mature plant creatures serve as leaders for their deadly cousins. They're stronger, tougher, and more deadly than the lesser plant creatures. They also have the ability to summon forth Swarms to further trouble their enemies."
// DisplayNames :
"P728913286" "Herder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Striga_Plant_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Striga_Plant_Beast_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Plant_Beast_Lieutenant_Hive 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Mushroom_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4144183863" "Fungus run amok' is probably the best way to describe these loathsome creatures. Like their inanimate ancestors, mushroom men prefer dark, dank places. In combat they can release clouds of deadly spores that choke and disable nearby enemies."
// DisplayNames :
"P3703635051" "Fungoid"
// DisplayNames :
"P888793680" "Deathspore"
// DisplayNames :
"P1180789635" "Deathcap"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Mushroom_Beast_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3947892750" "These horrid parodies of men lead the fungi armies of the Devouring Earth. Their pummeling attack can shatter bones while their spore clouds disable their victims. Meanwhile, their summoned Swarms hold other foes at bay."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Rock_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P156695829" "Made from assemblages of rocks that are somehow given form and consciousness, the Rock Troops are tough, resilient creatures who can either pound their opponents in close combat or hurl rocks from a distance."
// DisplayNames :
"P1820233972" "Bedrock"
// DisplayNames :
"P516410795" "Boulder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Rock_Beast_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4102879753" "The leaders of the Rock Troops are tougher, smarter, and better equipped to take on whatever foes the Devouring Earth sets them against. In addition to the rock wielding skills of their subordinates, they have the ability to summon forth deadly Swarms of insects."
// DisplayNames :
"P3604722071" "Sentry"
// DisplayNames :
"P336346884" "Granite"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Rock_Beast_Lieutenant_Hive 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Green_Crystal_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3825132196" "The Devouring Earth grows these crystalline warriors in special caves deep beneath the Earth. Their blasts of shards can cut deeply into a target's flesh and bone, and energy attacks have a diminished effect against their crystalline forms. Luckily, they're susceptible to smashing attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1607189276" "Geode"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Red_Crystal_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1749949894" "Quartz"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Black_Crystal_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P943532948" "Sardonyx"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Crystal_Beast_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3484670663" "These Crystal captains command their sparkling soldiers in combat, chattering amongst one another with voices like breaking glass. In combat they rain down shards of razor sharp crystal and pummel their opponents mercilessly. Like their followers, these creatures fear smashing attacks."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Swarm 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P751631938" "These nettlesome Swarms are sometimes encountered in groups, though they can also be summoned by other Devouring Earth creatures. They are highly resistant to smashing and lethal attacks, but theses flying hordes don't fare well when confronted with fire or energy based assaults."
// DisplayNames :
"P4208939798" "The Swarm"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Lesser_Devoured_Boss_01 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3055746710" "The Devoured were once normal human beings, but they have since been transformed into horrifying creatures. Their bodies have been mutated grotesquely, and even their brains have been perverted into believing the radical environmental precepts of the Devouring Earth. In combat they show their hatred for the world of men by spitting poison at their foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P3188123950" "Lesser Devoured"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Lesser_Devoured_Boss_02 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Greater_Devoured_Boss_01 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4012225622" "The ultimate eco-warriors, the Greater Devoured incorporate the biomass of fallen heroes into their monstrous forms. They rend foes with their slashing talons, spitting poison on those they can't reach. A Greater Devoured is a formidable foe, resistant to most kinds of attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P3623808169" "Greater Devoured"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Greater_Devoured_Boss_02 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Gaia 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1087730007" "Transformed by a Devouring Earth drug, this raging beast was once the woman Tanya Tyler. Now capable of breeding Devouring Earth creatures, Terra is the monsters' greatest offensive weapon in their war against humanity."
// DisplayNames :
"P2004905891" "Terra"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Jurassik 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3300204182" "The giant monster was dubbed Jurassik by a hero some time ago, and the name has stuck (though the hero has regrettably disappeared). It appears that Jurassik has been mutated by the many pollutants and chemicals in Crey's Folly. Now, it is a creature of pure violence."
// DisplayClassName :
// DisplayNames :
"P3237330354" "Jurassik"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarth_Jurassik_Monster 
