// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Axe_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2045581708" "The dregs of Freakshow society, the Freaks are newbies who haven't earned their metal yet. They have to prove themselves by using axes, bats, guns, and anything else they can get their hands on to cause as much damage as possible."
// DisplayNames :
"P4058151669" "Freak Chopper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Sledgehammer_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P68199725" "Freak Slammer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Shotgun_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P119305624" "Freak Buckshot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_SubmachineGun_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P544300140" "Freak Gunner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Axe_Mad_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3321621794" "Mad Freaks have earned their Excelsior Feeder, a device that pumps the drug directly into their bloodstream. That makes them stronger and tougher than humanly possible, as well as more than a little bit crazy."
// DisplayNames :
"P3935194978" "Mad Freak Chopper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Sledgehammer_Mad_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P528257210" "Mad Freak Slammer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Shotgun_Mad_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1768693578" "Mad Freak Buckshot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_SubmachineGun_Mad_Freaks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1306636345" "Mad Freak Gunner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Enforcers_Swipers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P849589479" "The Enforcers are what everyone thinks of when they hear the word Freakshow: dangerous punks with over-sized mechanical arms ending in nasty looking weapons. They are the true heart of the Freakshow, deadly in combat but not yet totally insane."
// DisplayNames :
"P1127074868" "Enforcer Swiper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Enforcers_Smashers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3224237299" "Enforcer Smasher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Juicers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2050434241" "Juicers undergo a very specific and unusual cybernetic enhancement, one that sets them apart from all other Freaks and does strange things to their brains. A network of electrical wiring and emitters allows the Juicers to shoot forth great gouts of electrical energy that can devastate their foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P2091364732" "Juicer Freak"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Stunner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3017659250" "Stunners undergo a very specific and unusual cybernetic enhancement, one that sets them apart from all other Freaks and does strange things to their brains. A network of electrical wiring and emitters allows the Stunners to immobilize even the strongest heroes for a short period of time."
// DisplayNames :
"P1389196058" "Stunner Freak"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Metal_Freaks_Swiper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1356595182" "The Metal Freak's devotion to the cause is obvious - he's had both arms replaced with robotic contraptions that are good only for destruction. He must rely on other Freaks to feed him, but in combat he is a whirling nightmare."
// DisplayNames :
"P2104455115" "Metal Swiper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Metal_Freaks_Smasher 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3977337309" "Metal Smasher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Enforcer_Swiper_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2330082560" "A combination of revolutionary fervor and massive doses of Excelsior allows the leaders of the Enforcers to completely ignore the effects of pain. This trait lets them keep on fighting when by all rights they should have dropped dead."
// DisplayNames :
"P1102493262" "Chief Swiper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Enforcer_Smasher_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1895823275" "Chief Smasher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Metal_Freak_Swiper_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1351216162" "These are the heroes of the Freakshow,  devoted utterly to smashing the state and having a great time while they're doing it. They're totally without care or mercy; point them in the right direction (or even the wrong one) and mayhem ensues."
// DisplayNames :
"P4180233285" "Champion Swiper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Metal_Freak_Smasher_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3885347289" "Champion Smasher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Tank_Freak_Boss_Swiper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P940112075" "The fully armored, incredibly tough Tank Freaks are a rare breed indeed. As their name suggests, they're almost unstoppable in combat. The one ray of hope when confronting a Tank Freak is that their electronics are not always top of the line, leaving them vulnerable to energy attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1055831790" "Tank Swiper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Tank_Freak_Boss_Smasher 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2790657091" "Tank Smasher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Juicer_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P36263716" "It takes some skill to control death dealing levels of electricity as they course through your nervous system, and Juicer leaders have that control. They can use their implants to generate massive balls of lightning. They're no fun in close combat either, as their punch packs a heck of an electrical wallop."
// DisplayNames :
"P2552547626" "Juicer Chief"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Stunner_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P170565946" "It takes some skill to control death dealing levels of electricity as they course through your nervous system, and Stunner leaders have that control. They can use their implants to fire bolts of electricity and even create fields of crackling lightning around their foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P3058568012" "Stunner Chief"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Clamor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P11562384" "Eve van Dorn's had a hard time finding friends as dedicated to violence as she is. For a while she found a home in the Council's previous regime, but she could only advance so far in such an organization. So she turned to the Freakshow. Under the name Clamor, Eve's had no trouble rallying other Freaks to her banner."
// DisplayNames :
"P4214746176" "Clamor"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Bile 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3841663379" "Ralph Francesco was an early members of the nihilistic group that would later become the Freakshow. his experience as an army veteran made it inevitable that he'd become one the organization's top men. Because of this lofty position, Ralph was one of the first to undergo cybernetic augmentation. Henceforth, he became known only as Bile."
// DisplayNames :
"P2748255865" "Bile"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Freakshow_Drek 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2225214582" "Born Daniel Watson, Dreck is the glue that holds the militantly independent Freakshow together. The Freaks may chafe at his orders, they may laugh at his haircut, but they all have to respect Dreck's absolute lust for violence."
// DisplayNames :
"P1892411644" "Dreck"

