// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Soldier 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P388409163" "Although Nemesis likes to dress his soldiers in 19th century style, their weaponry is decidedly modern. Most infantrymen attach their bayonets to special assault rifles that outperform all modern equivalents."
// DisplayNames :
"P3697722655" "Chasseur"
// DisplayNames :
"P4117714011" "Armiger"
// DisplayNames :
"P1524846578" "Lancer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Medic 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P617789741" "The Battle Surgeons are charged with the vital duty of getting wounded soldiers back into the fight as quickly as possible. Most Nemesis officers frown upon those who refuse to fight again; courage in the face of danger is highly valued in the Nemesis army ranks."
// DisplayNames :
"P2428324006" "Chasseur surgeon"
// DisplayNames :
"P2668356996" "Armiger surgeon"
// DisplayNames :
"P3570732531" "Lancer surgeon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Support 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3707283974" "The Nemesis army's main support weapon is the storm rifle, a long barreled weapon with a bayonet affixed to the end. It fires compact shells that carry a tremendous punch, exploding with the force of a heavy grenade or rocket shell."
// DisplayNames :
"P1348756198" "Carabineir"
// DisplayNames :
"P3177428538" "Fusilier"
// DisplayNames :
"P2825822225" "Grenadier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Sniper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P520149370" "At first glance, the Nemesis lance looks much like the spear from which it takes its name. Though it can be used as a spear, it's also a very powerful, accurate rifle. The Nemesis lance fires explosive rounds over long distances and requires great skill to use effectively."
// DisplayNames :
"P3095442629" "Lance Corporal Comet"
// DisplayNames :
"P160491803" "Subaltern Comet"
// DisplayNames :
"P1904835834" "Lance Sgt Comet"
// DisplayNames :
"P3468113506" "Sergeant Major Comet"
// DisplayNames :
"P3588671250" "Lieutenant Comet"
// DisplayNames :
"P2519090960" "Captain Comet"
// DisplayNames :
"P456946602" "Colonel Comet"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3529286796" "Nemesis' officers are some of the best trained soldiers in the world, and they show amazing discipline and devotion to their master. They're armed with the Nemesis lance, a long rifle that can also operate effectively as a spear. Their skill with this weapon makes them deadly at any distance."
// DisplayNames :
"P3187574657" "Lance Corporal"
// DisplayNames :
"P3613885629" "Subaltern"
// DisplayNames :
"P1390205858" "Lance Sergeant"
// DisplayNames :
"P55067869" "Sgt. Major"
// DisplayNames :
// DisplayNames :
"P1636337351" "Captain"
// DisplayNames :
"P812459191" "Colonel"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Elite 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3050944664" "The elite troops of Nemesis' army have tremendous discipline and skill that allows them to stand fast in the face of danger. They carry a deadly weapon that melds a scorching flamethrower with a powerful Gatling gun, giving them all the firepower they need for any foe."
// DisplayNames :
"P1047524647" "Cuirasseur"
// DisplayNames :
"P2385237392" "Hussar"
// DisplayNames :
"P1652884659" "Dragoon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Soldier_GasMask 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Medic_GasMask 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1593864506" "Chasseur Surgeon"
// DisplayNames :
"P1354161176" "Armiger Surgeon"
// DisplayNames :
"P459813999" "Lancer Surgeon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Support_GasMask 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Sniper_GasMask 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2083491420" "The Nemesis army's main support weapon is the storm rifle, a long barreled weapon with a bayonet affixed to the end. This seemingly simple weapon is actually quite versatile. The Tirailleurs have modified their weapons to fire poison gas grenades."
// DisplayNames :
"P2167271376" "Subaltern Tirailleur"
// DisplayNames :
"P3927341864" "Lance Sgt Tirailleur"
// DisplayNames :
"P2992756045" "Sergeant Major Tirailleur"
// DisplayNames :
"P2971781981" "Lieutenant Tirailleur"
// DisplayNames :
"P1816372352" "Captain Tirailleur"
// DisplayNames :
"P3605076835" "Colonel Tirailleur"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Lieutenant_GasMask 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Elite_GasMask 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Jaeger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3956205745" "Jaegers take their name from the German word for 'hunter'. They're some of the strangest and most advanced combat robots to ever stalk the streets of Paragon City. Nemesis seems to have a limitless supply of these steam-powered killers, each armed with powerful ranged or melee weaponry."
// DisplayNames :
"P1555202866" "Jaeger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Jaeger_Slicer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3031428209" "Gewehr Jaeger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Jaeger_Bomber 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1804057277" "Werfer Jaeger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis_Warhulk 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4116619885" "The War Hulk is the largest and most powerful killing machine built by the Prussian Prince of Automatons. It's a veritable walking tank, armed with flamethrowers, storm cannons, and an impressively brutal power claw."
// DisplayNames :
"P2216988219" "Warhulk"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Fake_Nemesis 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1131599923" "No one alive has ever seen Nemesis' true face. He hides within his finely wrought armor, safe behind personal force fields and a variety of armaments. He has many such suits of armor, each of which is a robot in its own right, capable of acting - and killing - independently."
// DisplayNames :
"P4186425052" "Fake Nemesis"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Prototype_Fake_Nemesis 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1664839274" "Prototype_Fake Nemesis"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_Nemesis 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1009570393" "Nemesis has had over 100 years to perfect his armor and his combat skills. He is a formidable, and wily, opponent."
// DisplayNames :
"P2545933599" "Nemesis"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nemesis_NemesisGas 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2857037096" "This poisonous gas was once a part of Nemesis' plot to conquer America. Though his plan to poison several major cities was thwarted, he still keeps large quantities of the gas around to help tip battles in his favor."
// DisplayNames :
"P3243557949" "Nemesis Gas"

