// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Cadaver 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2426475551" "These reanimated corpses give off a powerful stench that's a mixture of chemicals and rotting flesh. The odor becomes a hundred times worse when they use their favorite attack - vomiting a stream of corrosive acid on their nearby opponents."
// DisplayNames :
"P854767262" "Cadaver"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Embalmed_Cadaver 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3493584741" "These zombie-like constructs have numerous pieces of technological equipment protruding from their dead flesh. The purpose of all this machinery is to turn these creatures into walking bombs. When near a target, they explode to cause maximum damage."
// DisplayNames :
"P1858859413" "Embalmed Cadaver"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Reaper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1672753690" "The Reapers seem to be the only normal humans among the ranks of Dr. Vahzilok's reanimated legions. They are trained surgeons who collect body parts with the help of poison darts and industrial strength hacksaws."
// DisplayNames :
"P3502016422" "Reaper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Abomination 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2989888741" "In reanimation, as in cooking, better ingredients yield better results. Dr. Vahzilok constructs his Abominations out of the very best ingredients he can find: the organs of fallen heroes. The Abominations are stronger, tougher, and faster than their Cadaver kin. Unfortunately, they don't smell any better."
// DisplayNames :
"P47291683" "Abomination"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Embalmed_Abomination 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2314881753" "When an experiment doesn't work out the way he expected, Dr. Vahzilok doesn't complain. Instead, he makes the best of a bad situation, by converting the subject to a lethal weapon. The Embalmed Abominations are faster and tougher than their Cadaver counterparts, and they explode just as violently."
// DisplayNames :
"P3428585730" "Embalmed Abomination"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P325153569" "Mortificator"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Mire_Eidolon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3975850207" "In Dr. Vahzilok's mind, the Eidolons are mankind's next great evolutionary leap. Unlike the cadavers, they retain all of their memories and personality. The lucky few who can pay to become a Eidolon are augmented with the remains of heroes, so they often have super powers. Mire Eidolons have mastered the ability to control darkness itself. They tend to root their foes with tendrils of darkness and then launch into an attack."
// DisplayNames :
"P3693285427" "Mire Eidolon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Mire_Eidolon_Female 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Murk_Eidolon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P405976117" "In Dr. Vahzilok's mind, the Eidolons are mankind's next great evolutionary leap. Unlike the cadavers, they retain all of their memories and personality. The lucky few who can pay to become a Eidolon are augmented with the remains of heroes, so they often have super powers. Murk Eidolons, like the Mire Eidolons, have mastered the ability to control darkness. They tend to immobilize their opponents, then drain their life."
// DisplayNames :
"P2953682349" "Murk Eidolon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Murk_Eidolon_Female 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Luminous_Eidolon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2067663755" "In Dr. Vahzilok's mind, the Eidolons are mankind's next great evolutionary leap. Unlike the cadavers, they retain all of their memories and personality. The lucky few who can pay to become a Eidolon are augmented with the remains of heroes, so they often have super powers. The Luminous Eidolons toss blasts of radiation to weaken their foes; they are masters of long ranged attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P4288090129" "Luminous Eidolon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Luminous_Eidolon_Female2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Luminous_Eidolon_Female 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_DrVahzilok 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2064747104" "The insane leader of the Vahzilok comes across more like a religious zealot than an arch-fiend. Dr. Vahzilok continually proclaims his intention of overcoming death itself. In his twisted mind, the horrid reanimated corpses he creates are only stepping stones toward greater medical miracles."
// DisplayNames :
"P3945831726" "Dr. Vahzilok"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Nictus_Hunter_Reaper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1293208971" "Reaper Quantum Gunner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Vahzilok_Nictus_Hunter_Lieutenant 
